## Context

Scope step of PR 2438 (ticket 1519), filed by raid 075fa8 so that the
verify-gate's scope-overflow entry has its ticket. `trace_events.zstd_lines`
and `open_lines` split with `str.splitlines()`, which also cuts a JSONL record
at a raw U+2028 or U+2029 inside a JSON string. Measured by the 1519 executor
on 2026-11-10 (counts only): 84 unparsable lines on doudou's archive copy in
the audit window split that way, 0 when split on `\n`; 49 live padme
transcripts hold the character. trace-stats and trace_timeline read through
these helpers.

## Scope

The two helpers split on `\n` only (plain files opened with `newline=""`).
Readers of seat reports and other non-JSONL text keep `splitlines()`.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `zstd_lines` and `open_lines` split on newlines only, with tests for a
  U+2028 inside a record, CRLF and blank lines (PR 2438)
